body:
I think setting the OCICertPath and DockerCertPath to the same location is probably good for now.  However I wonder if the DockerCertPath should be set by Docker somehow and we should use that as a secondary lookup if there are no certs in OCI's location or they're invalid?

@mtrmac thoughts?  I'm on the fence.

Also this change creates the default certificate directory, but does doing this allow 'kpod pull' and 'kpod push' and others to use this directory without specifying the directory at the command line?  I think so via the code in /github.com/containers/image/oci/layout/oci_src.go, but would like to know if you tested that.

